    "intro_html":  "Hainanese chicken rice is Singapore\u0027s national dish and it is a masterclass in wasting nothing. You poach the chicken gently, then cook the rice in the poaching broth with garlic and ginger, so the grains carry every bit of flavor the meat gave up. The ginger garlic sauce on the side is what people actually dream about. Each bowl lands at 681 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e40 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.79 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
